James sought clarity and improvements on two summaries regarding the impact of climate change on GDP and labor productivity. He expressed concern over the wording "average person" and requested revisions to specify that the analysis is population-weighted, while also noting omitted issues like flooding, wildfire, and drought. I provided a clearer version of his GDP summary. James then requested a more neutral term to replace "heavily" in a statement about labor productivity influenced by temperature increases. I suggested "significantly" and offered alternative words like "notably," "considerably," "markedly," "substantially," and "strongly" to enrich his vocabulary.
